    test: two references restated for water's own compressibility (D27)
    
    Decision D27 (2026-10-16; forced, the owner was informed). After M2 the network's liquid water is the
    engine's (IAPWS-IF97 Region 1), no longer a flat 1e-9 1/Pa about a fixed density. Two runtime tests
    missed their bounds for that reason alone.
    
    CadenceTrajectoryQualificationTest: the reference pair is 0.25 s against 0.125 s (was 0.5 s against
    0.25 s).
    - Physics: two rigid 1 m3 tanks of 350 K water at 500 and 150 kPa equalise through a 10 km, 6 mm pipe.
      Each tank's pressure moves by dm/(rho V kappa), so the time constant is the pipe's resistance times
      rho V kappa / 2, proportional to kappa. Region 1 gives 4.56e-10 1/Pa at 350 K: the time constant falls
      from 56 to 25 s, and the first 20 s frame spans 0.8 of it.
    - Backward Euler's error grows with the step over the time constant: the old pair differed by 0.33 %
      in cumulative flow against the 0.25 % bound that checks the reference is converged. The new pair
      differs by 0.16 %.
    - The bounds are unchanged (0.25 % for the pair, 2 % for the cadences against the finer reference).
      The cadences lag the 0.125 s reference by up to 1.77 % (water, 20 s cadence; adaptive 1.45 %).
    
    McpGameplayRegressionTest: the clamped liquid-full island is re-archived under the current model.
    - Physics: the 2026-09-16 capture's tank held 55289.2 mol (996.05 kg) of water and 2.47e-4 mol of
      nitrogen in 1 m3 at 298.16 K and 150.66 kPa. Region 1's water there is 997.07 kg/m3, so this water
      fills 0.99898 m3. The tank therefore had a 1 L void, its wall went slack at 1 atm, and the replay's
      first 25 ms were a 1 L refill from the 200 kPa generator at 44 kg/s. The default and refined steps
      booked that refill differently: 0.64 % in the mean flow against the 0.2 % bound.
    - AGENTS.md: a changed material data set is tested on a fresh world, never an old one. The fixture now
      holds only the island's graph, regenerated by the current model. Each node keeps its captured
      temperature, pressure and minor components, and its major component fills its 1 m3. The tank holds
      the same nitrogen with 55345.42 mol (997.06 kg) of water; the generator holds 55347.04 mol; the
      nitrogen void and the pipes are as captured. The capture's clocks, history, anchor and status are
      gone: the test reads only the graph. No shim: the reader is unchanged.
    - The tank read from the fixture closes from its inventory to the captured temperature and pressure.
      Default and refined mean flows agree to 4e-6 % (1 accepted substep against 52). After 200 intervals
      of 5 s the nitrogen trace is 1.6e-17 mol, still positive.
    - mcp-held-drain-checkpoint.md records the re-archive; the held-drain checkpoint is unchanged.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

